// `str::sprintf` is declared `-> string` but returns a bare
// `Value::error(..)` when the format fails, and the two engines handle
// the type violation differently: the node-walk passes the off-type
// value through, the fused DynCall's return-shape check drops it.
//
//   interp: error:"MissingArg"
//   jit:    <nothing at all>
//
// Reachable from any format-string mistake — a missing argument (this
// program), a bad conversion (`str::sprintf("%s", i64:1)` ->
// error:"BadArgType"), or an unknown verb. A WELL-TYPED call agrees in
// both modes (`str::sprintf("%d", i64:1)` -> "1"), so the divergence is
// confined to the error path. It also survives being consumed: with
// `{ let e = str::sprintf("%d"); let r = { let s = "<[e]>"; s }; r }`
// the interp emits `<error:"MissingArg">` and the jit emits nothing.
//
// Chain, all verified in-tree:
// - stdlib/graphix-package-str/src/graphix/mod.gx:32 declares
//   `|fmt: string, @args: Any| -> string 'str_sprintf`.
// - stdlib/graphix-package-str/src/lib.rs ~792 returns
//   `Some(Value::error(ArcStr::from(e.to_string())))` on a printf
//   failure. It is the only bare-`-> string` builtin in the tree that
//   can produce a non-String Value; every other fallible str function
//   (sub/escape/unescape/splitn/parse) is declared as a Result union,
//   whose Nullable ABI carries an error through a kernel unmolested.
// - The node-walk has no shape check, so the Error flows on through the
//   string-typed binding and is observable (`is_err(a)` is true).
// - fusion/emit/call.rs ~321-345 sets `expected_disc = STRING` for a
//   String return and branches a non-matching disc into the pend block,
//   where the returned Value is DROPPED and replaced with a tainted
//   empty-ArcStr placeholder — the kernel then forces bottom. The
//   cross-region path does the same (fusion/kernel.rs ~1540-1552:
//   `mismatch(v)` substitutes a tainted empty ArcStr).
//
// Fix belongs in the stdlib, not the emitter — the emitter's check is
// what stops an Error payload word being adopted as ArcStr bits (that
// UB is exactly qop-bare-error-jul2026 and
// result-union-nullable-abi-aug2026). Declare the honest type:
//   let sprintf = |fmt: string, @args: Any| -> [string, Error<`FormatError(string)>]
// and tag the error with `errf!(literal!("FormatError"), "{e}")`,
// matching the other fallible str builtins. Both engines then agree and
// `?`/`$`/select can handle it.
//
// Worth taking at the same time: make the return-shape mismatch LOUD.
// call.rs's own comment calls a wrong-shaped dispatcher return "a
// compiler bug", yet it is reachable today from a stdlib signature bug
// and is completely silent. Log once, or refuse to fuse at discovery
// time when a Sync builtin's declared return is String/Array — at
// minimum this class should not silently lose a value. A sweep for
// other `EvalCached::eval` bodies returning `Value::error` under a
// non-union declared return type is warranted; this one was found by
// reading, not by the oracle.
str::sprintf("%d")
